{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Dāsaka","html":"<article id='thag1.17'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.17 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.17 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dāsakattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Dāsaka </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Middhī yadā hoti mahagghaso ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who gets drowsy from overeating, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Niddāyitā samparivattasāyī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fond of sleep, rolling round the bed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mahāvarāhova nivāpapuṭṭho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a great hog stuffed with grain: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Punappunaṁ gabbhamupeti mando”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that dullard returns to the womb again and again. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Dāsako thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
